pes of Google ads are:<br\/>- Display advertising<br\/>- Paid search advertising<br\/>- Social media advertising","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/google-ads\/#faq-question-1746689303125","position":2,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/google-ads\/#faq-question-1746689303125","name":"What is Google Ads?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Google Ads is an online advertising platform that allows businesses to run paid ads on Google\u2019s search engine and partner websites.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/google-ads\/#faq-question-1746689335391","position":3,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/google-ads\/#faq-question-1746689335391","name":"How does Google Ads work?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"By using Google Ads, marketers can bid on profitable keywords, and Google will show their ads based on relevance, quality score, and bid amount.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/google-ads\/#faq-question-1714828546632","position":4,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/google-ads\/#faq-question-1714828546632","name":"How do I use Google Ads to my advantage?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"- Reach your marketing goals<br\/>- Target your ads with keywords<br\/>- Get specific about your target audience<br\/>- Only pay for results<br\/>- Measure your ad's performance<br\/>- Advertise across platforms","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/google-ads\/#faq-question-1714828586858","position":5,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/google-ads\/#faq-question-1714828586858","name":"What is the minimum time required on Google Ads?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"At least 30 minutes per week are recommended to review the ad results and make required adjustments.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/google-ads\/#faq-question-1714828595652","position":6,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/google-ads\/#faq-question-1714828595652","name":"Can I goal distinct places with Google Ads?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, Google Ads allows advertisers to target unique geographic locations, from countries and regions to towns and neighborhoods.<br\/>","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/google-ads\/#faq-question-1746689352914","position":7,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/google-ads\/#faq-question-1746689352914","name":"What are the different Google Ads campaigns?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Common Google Ads campaigns are:<br\/>-<strong>Display Ads<\/strong> (Image ads on websites)<br\/>-<strong>Performance Max Ads<\/strong> (Multi-channel automated ads)<br\/>-<strong>Search Ads<\/strong> (Text ads on Google search results)<br\/>-<strong>Shopping Ads<\/strong> (For e-commerce products)<br\/>-<strong>Video Ads<\/strong> (YouTube ads)<br\/>-<strong>App Ads<\/strong> (To promote mobile apps)","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/google-ads\/#faq-question-1746689410295","position":8,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/google-ads\/#faq-question-1746689410295","name":"How much does Google Ads cost?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The cost of Google Ads campaigns may vary based on competition, keywords, and bidding strategy. So, set your daily budget to control overspending.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/google-ads\/#faq-question-1746689482558","position":9,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/google-ads\/#faq-question-1746689482558","name":"What is CPC, CPM, and CPA in Google Ads?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"-<strong>CPC (Cost Per Click) <\/strong>requires you to pay only when someone clicks on your ad.<br\/>-<strong>CPM (Cost Per Thousand Impressions) <\/strong>requires you to pay for every 1,000 ad views.<br\/>-<strong>CPA (Cost Per Acquisition) <\/strong>requires you to pay when a user completes a specific action, like a purchase or signup.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/google-ads\/#faq-question-1746689506990","position":10,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/google-ads\/#faq-question-1746689506990","name":"What is a Quality Score in Google Ads?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Quality Score (1 - 10) is measured based on ad relevance, keyword quality, and landing page experience. Higher scores often result in lower costs and better rankings.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/google-ads\/#faq-question-1746689520887","position":11,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/google-ads\/#faq-question-1746689520887","name":"How can we target the right audience through Google Ads?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Google Ads lets you target the audience according to keywords, location, demographics, interests, and behaviors.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/google-ads\/#faq-question-1746689536860","position":12,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/google-ads\/#faq-question-1746689536860","name":"What are negative keywords in Google Ads?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Negative keywords are used in Google Ads tactic to prevent ads from showing for irrelevant